        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And ye also, my children, observe the commandments of your father Enoch, and eat no blood, and observe the path of righteousness.&#x27; Noah cites his great-grandfather ENOCH as a normative source for his sons — Enoch is preached as PRE-MOSAIC patristic authority. **Tewahedo inter-canonical witness**: Jubilees and 1 Enoch mutually authorise each other within the Tewahedo canon — Jubilees cites Enoch (here and at 21:10), and 1 Enoch grounds the cosmology Jubilees presupposes. This mutual citation is unique to the Tewahedo/Eritrean Orthodox biblical structure.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 7:34 (Noah's commandments), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
