        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;For thus Enoch, the father of your father, commanded Methuselah, his son, and Methuselah his son Lamech, and Lamech commanded me all the things which his fathers commanded him.&#x27; Noah preserves a CHAIN OF TRANSMISSION — Enoch → Methuselah → Lamech → Noah — for the pre-Mosaic priestly halakhah. **Tewahedo apostolic-succession antecedent**: the chain-of-transmission motif (commandment passed from father to son across the generations) is a structural Tewahedo motif applied to the apostolic succession of the priesthood — bishops trace authority through unbroken succession that mirrors the Enoch-to-Noah pattern.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 7:39 (Noah's commandments), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
