        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And he knew that the Garden of Eden is the holy of holies, and the dwelling of the Lord, and Mount Sinai the centre of the desert, and Mount Zion — the centre of the navel of the earth: these three were created as holy places facing each other&#x27; — the three holy mountains: Eden / Sinai / Zion. Tewahedo sacred-geography preserves this tri-mountain structure as central to its theological topology, with the Tewahedo qǝddǝst-qǝddusan (holy of holies) understood as a participation in the Edenic-Zion holy-mountain pattern.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 8:19 (Division of earth (8:19)), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
