        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And the Lord our God bade us to bind all.&#x27; God&#x27;s first response to Noah&#x27;s prayer is TOTAL binding — every demon is to be confined. **Tewahedo theological anchor**: the divine intention is full restraint of evil; the partial loosening (10:8-9 — Mastema&#x27;s petition granting 1/10) is a CONCESSION to fallen creaturely freedom, not an original-divine plan. Tewahedo theodicy reads this as the canonical structure of God-permits-bounded-evil-for-greater-good — evil is never original or necessary.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 10:7 (Demons + Mastema + Babel), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
