        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And He said: &quot;Let the tenth part of them remain before him, and let nine parts descend into the place of condemnation.&quot;&#x27; God grants Mastema&#x27;s petition partially — 1/10 of the demons remain free to harass humanity, 9/10 are bound. **Tewahedo numerical-bounded-evil anchor**: this 10%-bound, 90%-restrained ratio is preserved in Tewahedo demonological teaching as the divine bounding of cosmic evil — evil is NEVER unbounded, even when permitted; the tithe-pattern (1/10) signals that the demonic share is the inverse of the human tithe-offering.</p></aside>',
