        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Noah wrote down all things in a book as we instructed him concerning every kind of medicine. Thus the evil spirits were precluded from (hurting) the sons of Noah.&#x27; Noah WRITES the medical book — a written transmission of healing knowledge that is identified by Tewahedo tradition with the Mäṣḥafä Mädḫanit (Book of Medicine). **Tewahedo scribal-tradition anchor**: the writing-down of revealed knowledge by patriarchs (Enoch the scribe at Jub 4:23; Noah the medical scribe at 10:13; the heavenly tablets passim) establishes the priestly-scribal vocation as a divinely-instituted office, undergirding Tewahedo monastic scribal practice.</p></aside>',
