        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And the Lord sent a mighty wind against the tower and overthrew it upon the earth, and behold it was between Asshur and Babylon in the land of Shinar, and they called its name &quot;Overthrow.&quot;&#x27; The Tower is overthrown by WIND (rūaḥ / mänfäs) — the same divine wind/Spirit that hovered over Genesis 1:2 now reverses Babel. **Tewahedo Pneumatological anchor**: Acts 2 (Pentecost) reverses Babel&#x27;s confusion through the SAME Spirit — the Tewahedo reading of the Spirit&#x27;s action at Pentecost as the antitype of Jubilees 10:26 is sharper than in Western Christianity, drawing on the explicit Jubilees pneumatology that Western tradition lacks.</p></aside>',
