        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Abraham blessed Jacob and said: he shall walk in My ways, and his children shall walk in My ways, and his seed shall be a blessing in the midst of the earth. And let not the spirits of Mastema rule over thee and over thy seed to turn thee from the Lord, who is thy God from henceforth and for ever&#x27; — Abraham&#x27;s blessing of Jacob (his grandson) before Isaac&#x27;s own blessing, with explicit Mastema-repulsion clause. The Tewahedo grandparental blessing tradition preserves this pattern: the grandfather&#x27;s blessing of the grandson includes a Mastema-repulsion clause analogous to Jub 19:28. The Tewahedo baptismal-and-childhood liturgy retains a comparable formula in the priestly blessing of children.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 19:28 (Sarah's death + Rebekah (19:28)), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
