        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;For thus I have found written in the books of my forefathers, and in the words of Enoch, and in the words of Noah, concerning the blood, for in the sight of the Lord this is a great sin, that they should shed the blood of any soul&#x27; — Abraham instructs Isaac, citing &#x27;the books of Enoch&#x27;. **Jubilees treats 1 Enoch as authoritative source**, creating an inter-textual canonical witness inside the Tewahedo canon itself: Jubilees cites Enoch, both are Scripture, both are preserved uniquely in Ge&#x27;ez.</p></aside>',
