        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And the Lord gave Joseph favour in the sight of Potiphar, and Potiphar set him over all that he had, and the Lord prospered all that he did&#x27; — Jubilees preserves the Gen 39:2-3 prosperity-under-Joseph narrative. Tewahedo Joseph-as-Christ Holy-Week typology reads this verse as the canonical pattern: the rejected-righteous-brother prospers in the household of his Gentile master, prefiguring Christ&#x27;s victorious-rejection-vindication. The Tewahedo Holy-Week Wednesday commemoration (Joseph&#x27;s day) draws on this verse for the Christ-prefiguring-prosperity-in-affliction motif.</p></aside>',
