        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Joseph was strong and beautiful, and the wife of his master saw him, and she lifted up her eyes and saw Joseph, and she loved him, and besought him to lie with her. But he did not surrender his soul, and he remembered the Lord and the words which Jacob, his father, used to read from amongst the words of Abraham&#x27; — Joseph remembers ABRAHAM&#x27;S TEACHING (transmitted through Jacob&#x27;s reading). Tewahedo wisdom-transmission tradition preserves this multi-generational scriptural-reading pattern: each generation reads aloud what the previous taught — the Tewahedo monastic recitation tradition is in this lineage.</p></aside>',
