        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Tamar conceived, and she bore twin sons; and she called the name of the one Perez, and the name of the other Zerah&#x27; — Jubilees follows the Gen 38 narrative of Perez and Zerah. The Tewahedo Christological-genealogy tradition: Perez is the ancestor of David (Ruth 4:18-22 = Mt 1:3) and ultimately of Christ. Tamar — the Canaanite-presumed-prostitute-daughter-in-law — preserves the Davidic-Messianic line through her courageous-faithful action where Judah faltered. The Tewahedo Marian-typology tradition reads Tamar (with Rahab, Ruth, Bathsheba, and Mary) as the four-women-in-the-Messianic-genealogy, each receiving canonical-pastoral honor as faithful-female-link-in-the-Messianic-line.</p></aside>',
