        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Joseph commanded that they should give them food when they had eaten, and he said unto them: Ye shall not return again until ye bring your youngest brother unto me&#x27; — the brothers&#x27; reunion sequence (parallel Gen 43:34, 44:23). Jubilees compresses but preserves the narrative; the Tewahedo lectionary uses Jubilees alongside Genesis for the Joseph cycle in Holy Week readings, drawing on the doubled canonical witness for the deeper Christological reading.</p></aside>',
