        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Israel went down into Egypt, into the land of Goshen, in the first year of the third week of the forty-fifth jubilee, in the second year, that is, the year in which Joseph was thirty years&#x27; — Jacob and Joseph reunited in Egypt, dated by jubilee. Tewahedo historical-chronological tradition uses the Jubilees jubilee-counting alongside the Genesis natural-year counting; both are canonical, neither subordinates the other.</p></aside>',
