        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And Joseph died being a hundred and ten years old; seventeen years he lived in the land of Canaan, and ten years he was a servant, and three years in prison, and eighty years he was under the king, ruling all the land of Egypt&#x27; — Jubilees gives the precise breakdown of Joseph&#x27;s 110 years: 17 + 10 + 3 + 80 (canonical biographical precision). Tewahedo monastic-biographical tradition (gədl genre) follows this precision-of-stages-pattern: each gədl of a Tewahedo saint enumerates the precise canonical-stages of the saint&#x27;s life (childhood + monastic-discipleship + spiritual-warfare + active ministry + death). The Tewahedo gədl literary form&#x27;s canonical anchor is the Jubilees-Joseph-biographical precision.</p></aside>',
