        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And after this law I made known unto thee the days of the Sabbaths in the desert of Sin which is between Elim and Sinai. And I told thee of the Sabbaths of the land on Mount Sinai, and I told thee of the jubilee years in the sabbaths of years&#x27; — Jubilees frames the book&#x27;s entire content as the divinely-revealed system of Sabbaths-AND-jubilees given to Moses on Sinai. The book IS Mäṣḥafä-Kufāle (&#x27;Book of Divisions&#x27;) — the canonical book-OF-divisions of time. Tewahedo liturgical-cosmology preserves Jubilees&#x27; Sabbath-and-jubilee structure as the canonical framework for the Tewahedo täzkar (commemoration) calendar: every Tewahedo täzkar is calculated using the Jubilees-Mosaic Sabbatical-of-Sabbaticals system, anchored in this verse.</p></aside>',
        "Jubilees 50:1 (Sabbath and Jubilee finale (50:1)), trans. R.H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (Oxford: Clarendon, 1902). PD.",
