        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;And the jubilees will pass by, until Israel is cleansed from all guilt of fornication, and uncleanness, and pollution, and sin, and error, and dwelleth with confidence in all the land, and there will be no more a Satan or any evil one, and the land will be clean from that time for evermore&#x27; — Jubilees presents an explicit eschatological-cleansing of the land, with Satan removed, and the land permanently clean. The Tewahedo eschatological-hope draws canonical anchor here: the final consummation is not merely individual-spiritual-resurrection but cosmic-territorial-cleansing-and-the-permanent-removal-of-demonic-presence. The Tewahedo distinctive emphasis on the consecration-of-the-land (the Tewahedo&#x27;s sacred-geography tradition that sees specific Ethiopian holy mountains and lakes as canonically-sanctified-territory) finds canonical anchor in Jubilees&#x27; jubilee-of-jubilees-eschatology.</p></aside>',
