        "Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition) (-150).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Jubilees (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of Jubilees (Mäṣḥafä Kufāle)</em> <small>(c. 150 BC)</small><p>&#x27;These are the words and the regulations regarding the sabbaths of the Lord, as they were written down for the children of Israel and the angels of God, that they may keep them, and not violate them throughout all their generations&#x27; — closing-sabbath regulations. Tewahedo sabbath theology (the historical Tewahedo observance of BOTH Saturday-Sabbath and Sunday-Lord&#x27;s-Day, unique among the major Christian communions until the 17th century — and still preserved in some monastic communities) draws on Jubilees 50 as canonical anchor for the centrality of Sabbath observance.</p></aside>',
